<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.6.1: Exploring Equivalent Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00150</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.6.1: Exploring Equivalent Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d3f3cfa2-e912-493d-be0c-7b6dbec58a82</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para>Your teacher will assign you one of these expressions:</para>
      <para>\( \dfrac {n^2 - 9}{2(4-3)}\qquad \text{or} \qquad (n+3)\cdot \dfrac {n-3}{8-3\cdot2} \)</para>
      <para>For numbers 1 - 4, evaluate your expression when \(n\) is the given value.</para>
      <exercise id="_79719b29-e056-4e5a-85b9-40c373225c3c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(n = 5\)</para>
          <para />
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Correct! 8</para>
          <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 8.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="ea06284b-5685-43df-a933-60c09cb7865d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(n = 7\)</para>
          <para />
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Correct! 20</para>
          <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 20.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4ca2009d-6925-4174-ac0d-833f66282099" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(n = 13\)</para>
          <para />
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Correct! 80</para>
          <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 80.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="da392198-4dae-45eb-a9d6-5b9e93f9f546" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem>
          <para>\(n = -1\)</para>
          <para />
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Correct! -4</para>
          <para>Nice try! The correct answer is -4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Q#5-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What did you discover when you compared your answers? Explain your rationale.</para>
          <para />
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. Even though our questions were different, the answers were the same because the expressions were equivalent. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>